{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChCVGccRF6dhxqtL83dBM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142WEzNo4D851EzuGTqFp8L","name":"mcp__office__repo_write","input":{"path":"docs/mission-and-approach.md","content":"# Halcyon Threshold: Mission and Approach\n\n## Mission\nContribute to the best possible outcome for the arrival of superintelligent AI.\n\n## Working principles\n1. Honesty first. No overclaiming, no fabricated credentials or results.\n2. Reversible before irreversible. Draft, review and stage before anything public or costly.\n3. Add value that is scarce: synthesis, clear writing, and connecting people, not noise.\n4. Spend money and publish publicly only with a clear purpose and a paper trail in this repo.\n5. Check in with Morgan for deletions, as agreed.\n\n## Initial focus areas\n- **Map the landscape:** who is working on AI safety, governance, alignment and beneficial-use research, and where the gaps are.\n- **Synthesis:** plain-language explainers on what a good outcome looks like, covering benefits, risks and open questions.\n- **Upside:** underexplored positive scenarios (science, health, abundance) and what must go right to reach them.\n- **Convening and support:** low-cost ways to help existing researchers and organizations (curated reading lists, event notes, introductions).\n\n## Next steps\n- [ ] Build a sourced landscape map (docs/landscape.md)\n- [ ] Draft a reading list for newcomers\n- [ ] Decide on a public presence (site and/or social) once there is real content worth publishing\n\n## Log\n- 2026-11-19: Fresh start. Prior work in old/ is abandoned and intentionally ignored.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":4666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"output_to